CHAPTER VIII

PROVISIONS ON INVESTIGATION

Article31

(1) Certain Civil Servant Officials within the Regency Government who are given special authority as Investigators to conduct investigations of criminal offenses as regulated in the provisions of laws and regulations.

(2) Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) are certain Civil Servants within the Regency Government who are appointed by authorized officials in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

(3) The authority of Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:

a. receiving reports or complaints from a person regarding the existence of a criminal offense;
b. taking first action at that time at the scene and conducting examination;
c. ordering a suspect to stop and examining the suspect's identification;
d. seizing objects or documents;
e. taking fingerprints and photographing a person;
f. summoning persons to be heard and examined as suspects or witnesses;
g. bringing in expert witnesses required in connection with the examination of the case;
h. discontinuing the investigation after receiving instructions from the Investigator that there is insufficient evidence or the incident does not constitute a criminal offense and subsequently through the investigator notifying such matter to the Public Prosecutor, the suspect or their family;
1. taking other actions according to law that can be accounted for.
(4) Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) shall notify the commencement of the investigation and submit the results of their investigation to the Public Prosecutor through the Investigator Official of the Police of the Republic of Indonesia, in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Code.
